    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="16" relname="span">I think P22 is exactly right here.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="25" relname="conjunction">I've been using computer since the early DOS days</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="25" relname="conjunction">and have seen many different application design styles,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="26" relname="span">so certain things may seem more intuitive to me</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="24" relname="disjunction">because I have encountered similar things in the past</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="24" relname="disjunction">or I may be better at jumping to certain conclusions.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="22" relname="span">However, for newer users, the number of design philosophies that are truly intuitive to them is considerably smaller.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="17" relname="span">Intuitiveness is only relavent as a application description</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="19" relname="span">if it used with the right context.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="20" relname="span">Without appropriate contextualization, the term is meaningless</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="10" relname="concession">(other than, as P22 points out, a good marketing tool).</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="18" relname="conjunction">Because every person is different</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="18" relname="conjunction">and just about every application is different,</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="21" relname="span">intuitiveness as design measure becomes incalculable and therefore worthless.</segment>
        <group id="15" type="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="span"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="27" relname="span"/>
        <group id="18" type="multinuc" parent="14" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="8" relname="condition"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="9" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="17" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="1" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="7" relname="concession"/>
        <group id="24" type="multinuc" parent="26" relname="volitional-cause"/>
        <group id="25" type="multinuc" parent="4" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="26" type="span" parent="23" relname="span"/>
        <group id="27" type="span" parent="16" relname="evidence"/>
    </body>
</rst>
